.TH XS 1 "2026-10-10" "xs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xs \- parallel rsync work-alike
.SH SYNOPSIS AND OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: xsync [OPTION]... SRC [SRC]... DEST
  or   xsync [OPTION]... SRC
  or   xsync [OPTION]... SRC [SRC]... [USER@]HOST:DEST
  or   xsync [OPTION]... [USER@]HOST:SRC [DEST]

Options (same meaning as rsync):
 \-v, \-\-verbose            increase verbosity
 \-q, \-\-quiet              suppress non\-error messages
 \-c, \-\-checksum           skip based on checksum, not mod\-time & size
 \-a, \-\-archive            archive mode; equals \-rlptgoD
 \-r, \-\-recursive          recurse into directories
 \-d, \-\-dirs               transfer directories without recursing
 \-R, \-\-relative           preserve source path components and implied directories
     \-\-files\-from=FILE    select source names from FILE ("\-" reads stdin)
     \-\-list\-only          list source entries; do not transfer or change DEST
 \-X, \-\-xattrs             preserve extended attributes (twice includes rsync internals)
 \-H, \-\-hard\-links         preserve hard links within the transferred tree
 \-S, \-\-sparse             create holes for zero\-filled file regions
     \-\-link\-dest=DIR       reuse unchanged files from a previous snapshot
 \-l, \-\-links              copy symlinks as symlinks
     \-\-safe\-links         skip symlinks that point outside the transfer tree
 \-L, \-\-copy\-links         transform symlink into referent file/dir
 \-p, \-\-perms              preserve permissions
     \-\-chmod=CHMOD        change incoming file/directory permissions
 \-E, \-\-executability      preserve executability of regular files
     \-\-fileflags          preserve BSD file flags (macOS)
 \-o, \-\-owner              preserve owner (super\-user only)
 \-g, \-\-group              preserve group
     \-\-chown=USER:GROUP   change destination owner/group (names or IDs)
 \-D                       same as \-\-devices \-\-specials
 \-A, \-\-acls               preserve ACLs (implies \-\-perms)
 \-t, \-\-times              preserve modification times
 \-U, \-\-atimes             preserve file access times (twice enables \-\-open\-noatime)
 \-N, \-\-crtimes            preserve creation times (macOS)
     \-\-open\-noatime       avoid read access\-time updates where supported
 \-O, \-\-omit\-dir\-times     omit directory modification/access/creation times
 \-J, \-\-omit\-link\-times    omit symlink modification/access/creation times
 \-n, \-\-dry\-run            perform a trial run with no changes made
 \-W, \-\-whole\-file         send the whole file; disable resume and block matching
     \-\-no\-whole\-file      enable verified\-prefix resume again
 \-x, \-\-one\-file\-system    don't cross filesystem boundaries
 \-e, \-\-rsh=COMMAND        specify the remote shell to use
     \-\-rsync\-path=PROGRAM specify the xsync to run on the remote machine
     \-\-no\-fallback        fail instead of re\-executing rsync for missing support
     \-\-fallback           enable fallback (overrides XSYNC_FALLBACK=0)
     \-\-existing           skip creating new files on receiver
     \-\-ignore\-existing    skip updating files that exist on receiver
     \-\-delete             delete extraneous files from dest dirs
     \-\-delete\-after       scan deletions and merge files after transfer
 \-m, \-\-prune\-empty\-dirs    omit empty directory chains from the file list
     \-\-delete\-excluded    also delete excluded files from dest dirs
     \-\-ignore\-errors      delete even when the sender encountered I/O errors
     \-\-max\-delete=NUM     delete at most NUM entries (exit 25 if exceeded)
     \-\-force              force deletion of dirs even if not empty
     \-\-max\-size=SIZE      don't transfer any file larger than SIZE
     \-\-min\-size=SIZE      don't transfer any file smaller than SIZE
     \-\-bwlimit=RATE       limit bytes sent/copied per second (bare RATE: KiB/s)
     \-\-timeout=SECONDS    remote idle I/O timeout (0 disables; exits with code 30)
     \-\-partial            keep partially transferred files
     \-\-inplace            update destination files in\-place
     \-\-mkpath             create the destination's path component
     \-\-numeric\-ids        don't map uid/gid values by user/group name
 \-u, \-\-update             skip files that are newer on the receiver
 \-I, \-\-ignore\-times       don't skip files that match size and time
     \-\-size\-only          skip files that match in size
 \-@, \-\-modify\-window=NUM  set the accuracy for mod\-time comparisons
 \-z, \-\-compress           compress file data during the transfer (zstd)
     \-\-compress\-level=NUM explicitly set compression level
 \-f, \-\-filter=RULE        add a file\-filtering RULE
 \-F                       merge .rsync\-filter files (twice also excludes them)
 \-C, \-\-cvs\-exclude        exclude CVS defaults and .cvsignore patterns
     \-\-exclude=PATTERN    exclude files matching PATTERN
     \-\-exclude\-from=FILE  read exclude patterns from FILE
     \-\-include=PATTERN    don't exclude files matching PATTERN
     \-\-include\-from=FILE  read include patterns from FILE
 \-0, \-\-from0              use NUL delimiters in list and filter merge files
     \-\-stats              give some file\-transfer stats
 \-h, \-\-human\-readable     use 1000\-based units (\-hh uses 1024)
     \-\-progress[=json]    show progress (default on terminals), or JSON events
     \-\-no\-progress        suppress progress; XSYNC_PROGRESS=0 also disables it
 \-P                       same as \-\-partial \-\-progress
 \-i, \-\-itemize\-changes    output a change\-summary for all updates
 \-8, \-\-8\-bit\-output       retain high bytes in names; escape unsafe control bytes
     \-\-out\-format=FORMAT  file lines: %i %n %L %l %o %f %b %t %% (optional width)
     \-\-log\-file=FILE      append the same stdout stream to FILE
     \-\-version, \-\-help

Documented compatibility no\-ops:
 \-s, \-\-protect\-args, \-\-secluded\-args
                          paths always travel as protocol data, not shell text
     \-\-blocking\-io, \-\-no\-blocking\-io
                          transport polling handles either pipe mode internally
     \-\-no\-motd            no daemon transport or daemon greeting exists

xsync extensions:
     \-\-install=HOST       explicitly install the matching release at ~/.local/bin
                          refuses newer versions unless \-\-force is supplied
 \-j, \-\-jobs=N             number of worker threads (default: performance cores)
     \-\-no\-clone           always copy file data, even where a copy\-on\-write clone
                          (APFS, same volume, with \-pt) would be possible
     \-\-atomic             create new files via temp file + rename (default)
     \-\-no\-atomic          create new byte\-copied files directly (fewer renames;
                          a crash can leave truncated files under final names)
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
XSYNC_FALLBACK
Set to 0 to disable automatic rsync fallback. The --fallback flag overrides it.
.TP
XSYNC_OPTS
Shell-quoted default options. Command-line flags override these defaults.
.TP
XSYNC_CONFIG
Optional defaults file; an empty value disables config. Otherwise the default
is $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xsync/config or ~/.config/xsync/config. Config options are
lower priority than environment defaults. Blank lines and full-line comments
are allowed. Transfer paths and control actions are not defaults.
.TP
XSYNC_RSH
Remote shell command, overriding RSYNC_RSH and default options; --rsh wins.
.TP
RSYNC_RSH
Remote shell command when --rsh and XSYNC_RSH are absent.
.TP
XSYNC_REMOTE_PATH
Additional remote executable path, after PATH and ~/.local/bin/xs.
.TP
XSYNC_RELEASE_DIR
Directory containing release artifacts for the explicit --install command.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Native peers support the current protocol and its predecessor. Missing remote
helpers, unsupported protocol versions and unsupported options use real rsync
from PATH unless fallback is disabled. Transfers never upload an executable.
.SH SEE ALSO
rsync(1), ssh(1)
